WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.293
(playful piano music)

00:00:01.293 --> 00:00:02.900
- [Narrator] Curious George,
the beloved children's book

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.915
character is a mischievous monkey

00:00:04.915 --> 00:00:08.292
who's inquisitiveness gets
him in all kinds of trouble.

00:00:08.292 --> 00:00:10.379
But before he reached global fame,

00:00:10.379 --> 00:00:12.492
George started as a drawing in the basket

00:00:12.492 --> 00:00:16.242
of a jerry-rigged bicycle
escaping the Nazi's.

00:00:18.171 --> 00:00:20.903
(bicycle bell dings)

00:00:20.903 --> 00:00:22.856
(Latin beat music)

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:26.087
It's 1935 in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil.

00:00:26.087 --> 00:00:28.234
Jewish-German artists and newlyweds

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:29.966
Margret Waldstein and Hans Reyersbach

00:00:29.966 --> 00:00:32.396
were living in an apartment
with two pet monkeys

00:00:32.396 --> 00:00:34.411
that were always causing trouble.

00:00:34.411 --> 00:00:35.351
(French bistro music)

00:00:35.351 --> 00:00:37.361
On their honeymoon in
Paris, Hans and Margaret

00:00:37.361 --> 00:00:38.592
fell in love with the city

00:00:38.592 --> 00:00:40.111
and decided to move there.

00:00:40.111 --> 00:00:41.336
They spent the next four years

00:00:41.336 --> 00:00:43.901
writing and illustrating children's books.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.777
One character was inspired by their pets

00:00:45.777 --> 00:00:48.360
in Brazil, a monkey named Fifi.

00:00:50.255 --> 00:00:52.439
(dramatic music)

00:00:52.439 --> 00:00:54.334
But World War II was underway,

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:57.820
and in May 1940, Nazi
Germany crossed into France

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.410
with their sights set on Paris.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.268
Hans and Margret planned
to escape to New York

00:01:02.268 --> 00:01:04.852
on a ship leaving for Lisbon, Portugal,

00:01:04.852 --> 00:01:07.877
but there were no more
trains out of Paris.

00:01:07.877 --> 00:01:10.229
After a desperate search
for transportation,

00:01:10.229 --> 00:01:11.892
they finally found a bicycle store

00:01:11.892 --> 00:01:13.685
that was nearly empty.

00:01:13.685 --> 00:01:15.620
Hans had to improvise.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.146
So he bought spare parts

00:01:17.146 --> 00:01:20.108
and cobbled together
two makeshift bicycles.

00:01:20.108 --> 00:01:21.529
The next morning Hans and Margret

00:01:21.529 --> 00:01:24.400
loaded their bicycles with
as much as they could carry,

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.568
including of course,

00:01:25.568 --> 00:01:28.868
their manuscripts for
the Adventures of Fifi.

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:31.076
They pedaled south for four full days

00:01:31.076 --> 00:01:33.356
to the nearest working train station,

00:01:33.356 --> 00:01:34.756
finally arriving in Lisbon

00:01:34.756 --> 00:01:37.589
to board a ship to Rio de Janeiro.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.603
(gentle music)

00:01:41.603 --> 00:01:43.248
From Rio, Hans, Margaret and Fifi

00:01:43.248 --> 00:01:46.089
were able to safely
board a ship to New York.

00:01:46.089 --> 00:01:49.102
It was here that they
published Fifi's first book,

00:01:49.102 --> 00:01:50.621
but decided to give him a new,

00:01:50.621 --> 00:01:53.573
more American name, George,

00:01:53.573 --> 00:01:54.823
Curious George.

00:01:55.742 --> 00:01:58.626
After the war, Hans and
Margret became US citizens,

00:01:58.626 --> 00:02:01.658
happily living out their
days in the States.

00:02:01.658 --> 00:02:04.017
And George, his story isn't over.

00:02:04.017 --> 00:02:06.809
The little monkey has
sold 75 million books,

00:02:06.809 --> 00:02:09.461
has been translated
into over 15 languages,

00:02:09.461 --> 00:02:10.986
and has his own TV show

00:02:10.986 --> 00:02:13.594
and three full-length movies.

00:02:13.594 --> 00:02:15.792
But most importantly,
he continues to delight

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:18.625
curious children around the world.

